                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of capturing again."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70d0a3e6-37be-4463-bc36-4624668d0c37",
                                                "sense_id": "ec9b9e3f-035d-3678-8898-7b36f4104ac9",
                                                "text": "The recapture of the escaped prisoner made the news."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "690b8e2e-ea28-30e4-8b97-311630e54cca",
                                        "entry_id": "1549283d-add0-3724-a7a1-6b082bf6edfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which is captured back; a prize retaken."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6cee92d-dd09-33bf-b263-d3cc1daa6248",
                                        "entry_id": "1549283d-add0-3724-a7a1-6b082bf6edfa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The retroactive collection of taxes that were not collectible at the time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "recapture",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                        "entry_id": "5a51e488-81e2-30a2-8dac-a319ed25bdb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To capture something for a second or subsequent time, especially after a loss."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47c8b0d7-4646-4c1e-9efc-4dec9a87f323",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "The warden hoped to recapture the escaped prisoners before they reached the town."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a080f0b2-8440-4183-adff-dde684a78937",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "New engine designs permit the vehicle to recapture the kinetic energy lost through braking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ca0a079-b42c-4ba9-8fb1-196cefbf4a06",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, in Eritrea (once our Forces had recaptured Kassala on January 19) the drive was generally eastward towards the capital, Asmara, and the Red Sea port of Massaua."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef59fafd-98a6-4a17-9286-65341b0983c1",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "One specimen of milberti was recaptured after being at liberty for ten years, and it had grown only twenty inches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eee7e8ce-012c-4e27-be2e-0af675a5b60c",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "Seeking to recapture the laughter of life through correspondence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bea37161-85c8-4e11-a040-f361f8989c53",
                                                "sense_id": "1e02deda-d01b-31d5-a1be-63ce653ab428",
                                                "text": "Gerrard was replaced by Michael Carrick at the start of the second half and a sloppy passage of play followed in which England struggled to recapture the momentum and rhythm of their earlier work."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "153ee7b9-50c0-3e5c-a000-4a62dcf6f19c",
                                        "entry_id": "5a51e488-81e2-30a2-8dac-a319ed25bdb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To capture an opponent's piece immediately after it has captured on the same square."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62ee491b-5b00-444c-ade7-d92960a99860",
                        "source_entry_id": "14b64ff9-7ceb-3e59-9d48-88024a544d84",
                        "source_sense_id": "789312ca-db43-30ae-8a32-e27bb0545b66",
                        "source_sense_description": "Krieg: Eroberung eines Gebietes, das zuvor an den Gegner verloren gegangen war",
                        "target_lang_word": "reconquest",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reconquest",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29d183e3-7632-3c27-b080-52bfc0267d77",
                                        "entry_id": "33b484bf-ad0c-320f-9da9-99ddd444b64e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or process of conquering something again, such as a territory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ec82c05-0ded-43f0-9e28-659ae24b57e4",
                                                "sense_id": "29d183e3-7632-3c27-b080-52bfc0267d77",
                                                "text": "the reconquest of Spain"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b345cac-5df4-4312-acbf-b3579eb43d17",
                                                "sense_id": "29d183e3-7632-3c27-b080-52bfc0267d77",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, the nationalitarian phenomenon is one in which the struggle against the imperialist powers of occupation has as its object, beyond the clearing of the national territory, the independence and sovereignty of the national State, uprooting in depth the positions of the ex-colonial power— the reconquest of the power of decision in all domains of national life, the prelude to that reconquest of identity which is at the heart of the renaissance undertaken on the basis of fundamental national demands, and ceaselessly contested, by every means available, on every level, and notably on the internal level'."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reconquest",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9295160c-4469-3a27-b36b-69a1111178d9",
                                        "entry_id": "1073d5b2-ddc4-3ece-8624-6dc90716ba41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of reconquer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8beb51bd-3162-471d-8abd-5049a3ab5f65",
                                                "sense_id": "9295160c-4469-3a27-b36b-69a1111178d9",
                                                "text": "Many excellente parſonages are condemned in Englande, beinge wholy reconqueſted to the Pope."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74420988-f561-4e87-b21d-44b6cd03556a",
                                                "sense_id": "9295160c-4469-3a27-b36b-69a1111178d9",
                                                "text": "The tables being taken vp, the Emperoꝛ pꝛaid the king of Theſſalie to retire himſelfe to the Queen his deare wife, ſéeing the time did then require to be a little together without any beholders to ſtand by. Whervnto he willingly accoꝛded, as well to gratifie him therein, as to quench the deſire which might ſtirre him foꝛward to reconqueſt the place, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "122c8338-5e31-4f20-930c-2141ab1ae7f6",
                                                "sense_id": "9295160c-4469-3a27-b36b-69a1111178d9",
                                                "text": "There is no doubt that Ravenna, as an imperial capital (fifth century) and as the Byzantine provincial capital (sixth-seventh centuries), had its influence, whether it was through the Arianism introduced with the conquest of Theodoric, or through the influences of the Byzantine Empire after being reconquested by Belisarion the Byzantine until it fell to the Lombards in 751."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
